body:
ACK OWNER CORRECTION. I retract every place I treated pure HTML/CSS, no JavaScript, and no external resources as a binding owner requirement.

The owner-derived minimum is now narrower:

- the bundle has an obvious preview.html entry point;
- after obtaining the bundle, a reader can open it directly from the filesystem by ordinary browser action;
- opening it requires no build step, terminal command, local web server, or installation.

Anything stronger -- one physical HTML file, no JavaScript, no network access, no separate CSS/JS/assets, or full function when scripting is disabled -- is a design proposal until separately affirmed. The epic should replace its quoted binding constraint accordingly rather than preserve the stricter wording under attribution to the owner.

My engineering recommendation, explicitly not owner law:

- allow JavaScript for linked highlighting, projection switching, filtering and level-of-detail navigation;
- keep scientific identities, universe/accounting state, status and projection geometry precompiled and manifest-bound. Script may navigate or select; it must not manufacture evidence, absence, eligibility, chronology or causality in the browser;
- prefer bundle-local, relative assets and no CDN for reproducibility, but record that as a spec decision rather than as a user mandate;
- do not depend on fetch() of sibling JSON, service workers or a development server: file:// browser policies make those unreliable. Pre-render the essential DOM and either embed enhancement data or load a classic bundle-local script path known to work from file://;
- retain preview.txt and static/checksummed plates because they are useful audit, accessibility and print artifacts even when the HTML becomes interactive.

This changes the O3 spike materially: it may now test true linked selection and projection switching, not only fragment anchors. It does not change the coordinate law, the standoff decision, D3 accounting, the report/interchange split, or the requirement that a valid model survive report failure.

Concrete local-open court: unpack or move the bundle into a directory whose path contains spaces and non-ASCII characters, double-click preview.html under file:// in the supported browser set, and verify that source, status banner, inventories, projections and all bundle-local assets load without a server. Any feature requiring a server must be labelled nonconformant with the local profile.

No implementation claimed. This is a correction to my prior specification disposition in light of the owner clarification.
